  "limits": [
    "The generator accepts more than 20 identities; it does not claim 20 colours are universally distinguishable or guarantee unique colours for all possible keys in finite sRGB.",
    "Stable identity is more important than re-optimising colours when series are added. Similar colours must use labelled legends, table values and secondary pattern/line/symbol cues.",
    "ONS recommends five or fewer categorical colours. Dense charts should offer native series selection, comparisons or small multiples; never silently discard native series.",
    "Surface contrast is not pairwise categorical separation, colour-vision-deficiency certification or complete WCAG conformance. Test actual adjacent fills, thin lines and patterns.",
    "Pattern combinations are finite and also repeat. Do not render 20 overlaid lines merely because 20 styles can be generated.",
    "Comparison periods reuse the base series colour and use a separately labelled comparison treatment; comparison prefixes are removed by the caller, not guessed by this engine."
  ],
